From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JSBedded <noreply@jsbedded.invalid>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/9] Add a generic ANT_EMBED profile under ANT_WASM_EMBED

Not sent upstream yet (upstream ask 1 in JSBedded's
firmware/engines/ant/README.md).

The interpreter-only build is tied to WebAssembly: wasm_embed.h stops
any other target with #error, and its host hooks are Wasm imports.
Microcontroller embedders need the same OS-free code paths.

- ANT_EMBED selects the OS-free paths that ANT_WASM_EMBED used to
  select (no mmap, libuv, tlsuv, argtable3, inspector or pthreads in
  the core). ANT_WASM_EMBED now requires ANT_EMBED and adds only the
  Wasm imports and exports.
- include/embed.h declares the hooks an embedder provides:
  ant_embed_now_ms, ant_embed_random_fill, ant_embed_should_interrupt
  and ant_embed_fatal (what a failed ANT_ASSERT does).
- js->wasm_interrupt_* become js->embed_interrupt_*, and
  ant_wasm_microtasks_reset becomes ant_embed_microtasks_reset.
- The Wasm reactor implements the hooks in packages/wasm/src/platform.c
  and builds with -DANT_EMBED=1 -DANT_WASM_EMBED=1. Its behaviour does
  not change.
